{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5, Anthropic's latest and most capable Sonnet model, which offers top-tier intelligence at Sonnet pricing for coding, agents, and everyday professional work at scale. This model delivers strong performance across various tasks, including coding, where it navigates large codebases, lands multi-file changes, and carries debugging and refactoring tasks through to completion with fewer rounds of correction. For agents, it calls tools precisely, holds state across many steps, and recovers from errors to ensure more runs finish correctly the first time. For knowledge work, it builds spreadsheets, drafts documents, and turns unstructured material into structured analysis. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and provides access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with AWS-managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. Claude Platform on AWS offers direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, allowing users to build, test, and deploy with the same APIs, features, and console experience as working with Anthropic directly, unified with AWS billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/06/claude-sonnet-5-now-available-on-aws/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5.5, an advanced and cost-effective Sonnet for coding and knowledge work. Sonnet 5.5 offers improved efficiency and faster processing compared to Sonnet 5. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5.5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure, offers regional data residency, and includes AWS-managed features like Guardrails and Knowledge Bases. Claude Platform on AWS provides direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, with unified billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/claude-sonnet-5-5-aws/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 is now in Amazon Bedrock - AWS","context":"Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 4.5 model is now available in Amazon Bedrock, a fully managed service offering high-performing foundation models from leading AI companies. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is Anthropic's most intelligent model, excelling at complex agents, coding, and long-horizon tasks while maintaining optimal speed and cost-efficiency. It leads the SWE-bench Verified benchmarks with enhanced instruction following, better code improvement identification, stronger refactoring judgment, and effective production-ready code generation. The model is ideal for powering long-running agents tackling complex, multi-step tasks, such as managing marketing campaigns or orchestrating enterprise workflows. In cybersecurity, it can help teams shift from reactive detection to proactive defense by autonomously patching vulnerabilities. For financial services, it can handle analysis to advanced predictive modeling. Amazon Bedrock API allows Claude to automatically edit context to clear stale information, and a new memory tool lets Claude store and consult information outside the context window to boost accuracy and performance. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is available in Amazon Bedrock via global cross region inference in multiple locations. To get started, refer to the News Blog, Amazon Bedrock console, Anthropic's Claude in Amazon Bedrock product page, and the Amazon Bedrock pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/anthropics-claude-sonnet-4-5-amazon-bedrock/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"Claude Sonnet 4.6 now available in Amazon Bedrock - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has added support for Claude Sonnet 4.6, a new model from Anthropic. Sonnet 4.6 offers improved performance and reliability for coding, agents, and knowledge work at scale. It is a direct upgrade to Sonnet 4.5 and is suitable for various use cases, including search and chat applications, agentic workflows, and domain-specific applications. The model delivers reliable performance at a lower cost compared to Opus 4.6 intelligence. Developers can use it for multi-model pipelines, and enterprise teams can leverage it for tasks requiring professional precision, such as spreadsheet and financial model creation, compliance review processes, and data summarization. Claude Sonnet 4.6 requires minor prompting adjustments for existing implementations and is now available in Amazon Bedrock. The model is suitable for high-volume deployment and maintains quality standards while optimizing for scale","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/claude-sonnet-4.6-available-in-amazon-bedrock/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search Bedrock billing documentation"}

